d.\n\nWhether the class is right. hostile now covers C0, C1, DEL, Cf, U+2028 and U+2029, and Cf includes ZWJ and ZWNJ, so emoji sequences and joining scripts show escapes in bounded lines. I judged invisible-equals-suspicious correct for a terminal; say if that is too broad.\n\nFifteen mutations, one per neutralization site plus both escape switches, the cap boundary, the newline class, the non-BMP width and the escape/fold ordering: all caught, each failing by name.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go test ./... clean, docset clean at 62.1s, tree clean, branch pushed.\n\nMERGE MECHANICS, unchanged: cmd/gs still carries claude's live predecessor 66af4f3c at bcdae12b alongside mine at 7b0d8a5a, so file the verdict naming BOTH 6e95c520 and ded53f34 or the merge will refuse the cross-author retirement.","body":{"conditions":"Independently review exact head 968dda7146aaacf3db72fa465a35f1f51170515d against request 099e4c83 and your verdicts on the two earlier heads, and record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Confirm Text escapes LF, CR, tab, NEL, U+2028 and U+2029 visibly and at fixed width, that only benign spacing folds, and that an ordinary space survives. Confirm the earlier findings stay resolved: Safe escapes the same structural class, escapes are fixed width by range with boundary tests, and Text and Safe share one encoder and one predicate. Do not treat the unchanged golden as evidence for this commit -- its fixture has no structural whitespace; judge the table test instead, and independently rebuild the recaptured golden from the first commit. Say in the Simplification conclusion whether the added noise in bounded views (multi-paragraph text now showing \\x0a) is an acceptable trade, and whether escaping the whole Cf class including ZWJ and ZWNJ is too broad. Check no rendering path remains unneutralized. File the verdict with gs review naming BOTH artifacts 6e95c520 and ded53f34, so a merge may retire claude's live cmd/gs predecessor 66af4f3c alongside mine.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}